WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.800
Movie. Flying with Butterflies.

00:05.800 --> 00:08.800
Um, hi there, I'm Lily and I'm...

00:08.800 --> 00:11.200
Well, I'm not really sure if I like science yet.

00:11.200 --> 00:13.000
It's kind of confusing, you know?

00:13.000 --> 00:15.200
But our classroom is pretty cool, I guess.

00:18.200 --> 00:22.000
In class, all these big words and numbers just make my head spin.

00:22.000 --> 00:24.200
I'd rather draw pretty butterflies.

00:24.200 --> 00:26.000
See? This is my notebook.

00:26.000 --> 00:28.400
More butterflies than science notes.

00:28.600 --> 00:32.600
Now, class, I have an exciting announcement to make.

00:32.600 --> 00:36.000
We're going to learn about something truly magical.

00:36.000 --> 00:40.200
Class, we're going on a field trip to the butterfly sanctuary tomorrow.

00:40.200 --> 00:44.200
You'll see hundreds of beautiful butterflies up close and personal.

00:44.200 --> 00:47.200
It's going to be an amazing scientific adventure.

00:50.200 --> 00:54.200
A butterfly sanctuary? Maybe science isn't so bad after all.

00:54.200 --> 00:56.200
I can't wait to see all those butterflies.

00:56.200 --> 00:59.200
Maybe I'll discover a new species and name it after me.

01:05.200 --> 01:08.200
Wow, it's like a whole new world.

01:16.800 --> 01:18.800
Wow, look at all these butterflies.

01:18.800 --> 01:20.800
They're even prettier in real life.

01:20.800 --> 01:24.800
Now, class, observe how the butterflies interact with their environment.

01:24.800 --> 01:27.800
It's a perfect example of ecosystem balance.

01:32.800 --> 01:35.800
Ooh, what's this machine? It looks important.

01:35.800 --> 01:37.800
Maybe I shouldn't touch it.

01:40.800 --> 01:42.800
Uh-oh. Whoa. What's happening?

01:42.800 --> 01:45.800
Everything's getting bigger. Or am I getting smaller?

01:45.800 --> 01:48.800
I can't believe it. I'm the size of a butterfly now.

01:48.800 --> 01:51.800
These wings are amazing. But how do I use them?

01:51.800 --> 01:53.800
Meep, meep, meep.

01:53.800 --> 01:55.800
Did that butterfly just talk to me?

01:55.800 --> 01:57.800
Um, sure, I'd love to learn.

01:57.800 --> 02:00.800
Maybe it'll help me figure out how to get back to my size.

02:02.800 --> 02:04.800
They're like tiny airplanes.

02:04.800 --> 02:07.800
Is that aerodynamics? This is amazing.

02:07.800 --> 02:09.800
The air currents, the wing shapes.

02:09.800 --> 02:11.800
It's amazing.

02:11.800 --> 02:13.800
Aerodynamics. This is amazing.

02:13.800 --> 02:15.800
The air currents, the wing shapes.

02:15.800 --> 02:17.800
It's all science.

02:18.800 --> 02:20.800
I'm doing it. I'm flying.

02:20.800 --> 02:23.800
I never knew science could be so magical and beautiful.

02:23.800 --> 02:27.800
Oh, no. I'm starting to grow back to my normal size.

02:27.800 --> 02:30.800
Goodbye, butterfly friends. Thank you for teaching me.

02:30.800 --> 02:32.800
Lily, where have you been?

02:32.800 --> 02:34.800
You look like you've had quite an adventure.

02:35.800 --> 02:37.800
Now I'm back to normal size,

02:37.800 --> 02:40.800
but I'll never look at science the same way again.

02:40.800 --> 02:43.800
It's like a key to unlocking the world's secrets.

02:43.800 --> 02:47.800
Let me tell you about the amazing things I learned about butterfly flight.

02:54.800 --> 02:58.800
And that's how I discovered that science isn't just facts and figures.

02:58.800 --> 03:01.800
It's a way to understand the magic all around us.

03:01.800 --> 03:05.800
So, who wants to go on a science adventure with me next time?

